00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
minimalism is about so much more than  just decoloring physical items from your  life it's about getting rid of the  excess so that you can make room for  what matters most to you in your life  but undoubtedly as your hobbies your  interests and just life in general  happens you will acquire more items and  so today i thought i'd take you along on  my monthly declutter and share with you  the 10 items that i'm going to be  declaring this month and why in case  you're feeling stuck in your  decluttering process or you just like to  start with minimalism and need some  ideas to figure out where to begin so  what i'll be doing is i'll first share  the item that i'm going to be getting  rid of and then i'll explain to you the  kind of category that you can look for  in your own home the first item on this  list for me is a faux leather case for  my pair of sheers now where this applies  to you would be pretty containers or  boxes for things that you purchase that  you don't need or you're not even using  but they're pretty boxes like your  iphone box you know a computer box that  you have lying around those sorts of  things you keep them because they're  good quality boxes and you don't want to  just throw them away but you're not  using them so in my case i had to  purchase a new pair of sheers this was  actually months ago because i do my own  hair my family's hair and i had kept the  case even though i could very well have  just put my shears in my own little  makeup pouch that saves me room it saves  me space and i don't have to get that  pouch and my makeup pouch when i'm doing  my eyebrows for example so look through  your house and look for any pretty boxes  or bags that you have no use for and  give yourself permission to get rid of  them the second one for me was actually  difficult for me to get rid of i went  back and forth and back and forth  whether or not i should do this and it's  unused electronics for me specifically a  gimbal for this youtube channel i had  purchased a very expensive gimbal the  zyun crane weeble lab i think it's  called and it is an awesome gimbal  however it didn't really fit my needs  for my lifestyle because it was  difficult to kind of balance it wasn't  difficult once i learned but it just it  required a lot of time and steps to take  it off the gimbal put it back on the  camera and maneuvering that with my kids  and my full-time job it just it didn't  work out i never ever used it because  it's so much easier for me to use this  selfie stick which i actually have right  here but it's extendable and it's  foldable and just so much nicely  in a bag versus having a gimbal while  carrying around kids and running after  them it didn't work and so i had to kind  of give myself the forgiveness that i  purchased this expensive item and didn't  use it so for you what this could be is  items that you have purchased and spent  a lot of money on but you know you're  not going to be using them sometimes  when we purchase really expensive items  and then we don't end up using them we  attach guilt to it and that's what keeps  us from getting rid of it to begin with  because we feel almost like we're gonna  lose money if we get rid of that item  but see the thing is we've already spent  that money that money's already gone so  what i did with my gimbal is i sold it  online of course i didn't make the same  amount of money that i paid for it to  begin with but at least i know that now  it will go to a home where it will  actually be used this next one is big  bulky furniture or furniture that you're  not using my husband had made this chest  well i guess it's a media console back  when we had a tv and he used to play  video games we don't have either of them  anymore and we didn't have a use for it  however we still had it up in our attic  for two years because hey maybe someday  we'll need it or maybe someday we'll use  it my sister had actually just moved out  recently and so we gifted it to her  sometimes though big bulky items if you  just keep them in your house you're  gonna find something to put inside them  and not only that but it's just causing  a lot of clutter in your home think of  the amount of space that they're taking  up that you could have opened up if you  would get rid of some of these items so  look around and see what kind of big  bulky furniture pieces maybe you can get  rid of this next one is a black fancy  dress it's one of those items that i  think it's just nice for me to look at  however i never really gravitate towards  because if i wear it i feel like i'm  maybe too dressed up or too  uncomfortable it's maybe a little too  snug here it's pretty to look at but i  don't wear it and so those sorts of  items really shouldn't belong in your  closet all the clothes that you have  should make you feel good should  accentuate the best parts of you try to  get rid of those maybe someday items  next we head off to the kitchen and this  is the category of food food that you're  never going to eat so i was recently on  the keto diet and i had purchased a  whole bunch of things specifically for  that that i didn't really end up using  and so i decided that i was going to  donate these to someone else that would  use them but look around too at things  that have been expired or things that  you bought because you were gonna make  that one specialty item and then you  realize yeah that's not gonna happen  consider getting rid of those this next  one for me is moonshine and i'm not  really one that really typically drinks  alcohol but i had recently been in  tennessee and tennessee is very well  known for its moonshine and because i  was on the keto diet at that time i  couldn't try it and they had a chocolate  coffee moonshine and i love chocolate  and coffee and i was just curious about  what they're well known for and so i  decided i'm gonna take one home and just  try it at home and see what it's like  and then i got home and i tried it it  just  it was strong stuff it just was not for  me and so i had kept it and i've tried  it and i'd sip it every now and then and  then i'd realize i'm not gonna drink  this this is not for me it's not my  thing i tried it okay i didn't like it  it's fine i can let it go so yeah i  poured it down the drain so i guess  where this can apply as a category for  things that you can look for in your own  home is those items that you decided you  were going to try but then you didn't  end up liking don't keep those if it's  not for you it's not something that you  enjoy give yourself permission to get  rid of it this next one is paper related  and i had recently gotten rid of our  vitamix recipe book because i realized  that i am not one that will typically  follow a recipe anyway and even though  this book was really beautiful and it  felt kind of soft on the front it had  beautiful pictures i realized if i'm not  ever going to use it i shouldn't just  keep it boxed up and taking up space in  our home and then also we have an  espresso machine that i had the manual  for manuals you can download pretty much  anything online or just look up a  youtube video on how to do something  which is typically what i go to that is  actually how i figured out how to clean  the machine was a youtube video maybe  it's not the wisest idea i don't know  let me know in the comments do you read  manuals or don't you these next two  items are old hobbies or things that i  know that i used to love that i don't  anymore so for me i used to really enjoy  chalk painting that furniture piece that  i actually showed you was one that i  painted and i enjoyed that i love that i  still really enjoy painting but not  shopping  painting homes renovating kind of thing  and so i had all of these paints that i  knew that i wasn't going to be using  because i hadn't used them in years and  so it was time for them to find a new  home and same thing goes with some cake  decorating supplies i had had an  assortment of things because i know how  to decorate cakes i had taken classes  before i can make flowers and pretty  designs and it's something that i  enjoyed years ago but it's not something  that i enjoy now i would much rather pay  somebody money to make me a cake now  than for me to make it myself it's just  not enjoyable anymore when i was getting  rid of these items it actually was it  was hard because it was almost like  letting go of a piece of my past and so  i had to kind of get around that by  telling myself getting rid of these  items doesn't mean that it's getting rid  of my past getting rid of my memories i  can still hold on to those memories take  pictures or videos of things that i have  done in the past and so i can keep those  without keeping the physical items so  maybe if you had hobbies that you no  longer enjoy consider maybe taking a  photo or video of them so that you can  kind of have a way to keep a memory of  them without actually keeping that item  this next category may not apply to you  but that is kids toys inevitably kids  just tend to acquire more toys even  though we haven't purchased toys for  them in a while and so periodically i  just kind of go throughout the house and  check for those toys that never get  played with if i do think that they just  haven't played with them in a while but  they may play with them again what i'll  do is i'll just box them up in a closet  for a few months and then take them out  and do what's called a toy rotation  where i take out some toys and give them  other toys that way i don't have so much  clutter and at the same time they get  kind of new toys every few months and  that is the 10 items that i am  decluttering this month i hope that in  sharing this it's been helpful to you  and given you some ideas of things that  you can get rid of so that you can make  room for what matters most in your life  thank you so much for watching if you  found this video helpful please give it  a thumbs up and subscribe so you won't  miss when i post a new video i'll see  you in the next one bye

